# Site block for the aviation API. Add it to the VM's existing Caddyfile once (paste it in, or
# `import /path/to/api.caddy`), then reload Caddy. Caddy must be attached to the "edge" Docker network.
#
# Everything is proxied: the API itself enforces API_TOKEN on GraphQL and POST /api/telemetry, and
# X-Admin-Token on DELETE /api/telemetry. WebSocket upgrades (GraphQL subscriptions) are proxied automatically.
# If Caddy runs on the host instead of in Docker, publish 127.0.0.1:8000:8000 on the api service and use
# `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000`.

api.sathishkottravel.com {
	reverse_proxy aviation-api:8000
}
